                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book'>Reliability: your confidence level of the numbers</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true' underline='true'>Educated Guess: </run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>A value derived from general business/market knowledge; </run>
                  <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true' underline='true'>Best Estimate</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'>: A value that is based on an estimation, such as the number of riders seen in a public place over time or the sequential IDs of competitor orders; </run>
                  <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true' underline='true'>Actuals:</run>
                  <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' italic='true'> You are reporting an actual number that reflects the competitor&apos;s internal data.</run>
