    <dashboard name='Methodology'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/OrderEstimationModel-DHUBtablesDevEnvironment/Methodology?rev=' id='Methodology' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/OrderEstimationModel-DHUBtablesDevEnvironment' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_3' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1440' minheight='800' minwidth='1440' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='88625' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98888' x='556' y='10375'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Stepwise Methodology:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>1. Leverage existing data sources about web, app traffic and search queries: Google, SimilarWeb and AppAnnie.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>2. Clean, transform, group and consolidate KPIs per market to use them as model features.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>3. Analyse their relationship to our orders. Example: in a given market, app sessions might correlate with our orders, whereas web sessions might not.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>4. Automatically detect when trends change in our data (e.g. COVID-19 or rebrandings) and define time windows.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>5. Extract meaningful features per competitor within each time window, based on data availability and their correlation to orders.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>6. Filter features based on Recursive Feature Elimination (feature selection method) in order to optimize performance.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>7. Apply dimensionality reduction to avoid cross-correlation and multicollinearity of features.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>8. Train a machine learning model to learn the relationship between features and our own orders in each time window, after removing outliers (e.g. marketing campaigns, public holidays, Ramadan).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>9. Based on the model performance, define confidence thresholds. Confidence is low if the model score is lower than 0.8, medium between scores of 0.8 and 0.9 and high if the model score is higher than 0.9.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>10. Filter out competitors with low confidence (not displayed in the dashboard).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>11. Apply the model learnings to the KPIs for competitors within the same market. Example: the model generated on Foodpanda in Taiwan is used to estimate orders of UberEats in Taiwan.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>12. Calibrate on local insights, such as financial reports or other publications.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>13. Adjust model estimates during holidays and Ramadan, based on their impact on the orders of our brands within the same market.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Notes:</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>1. Since we use indirect measures (app sessions, web traffic, etc.), we have to assume similar conversion rates between our brands and competitors within the same market. The magnitude is then fixed through model calibration (step 12.).</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>2. The report might experience some delay in case of input data lags (e.g. AppAnnie) and it will update as soon as we receive the new batch of data from providers.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>3. We arecontinously collecting local insights and feedback to refine our estimates with more information. Please reach out to DH Comp Intel </run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1155cc' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9' underline='true'>dh_comp_intel@deliveryhero.com</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> for further feedback.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Model Assumptions</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>If the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>OEM results change over time </run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>across different runs of the model, </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>yield high variance</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> between time periods, or </run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>stay far from other local estimates</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>, potentially, the important things are the</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> assumptions of the model</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>.</run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>The order performance of the local DH entity is used as the basis for the competitor estimates. This means that, the model assumes, if X number of downloads lead to N number of orders for DH, then X number of downloads should lead to N number of orders for the competitor. When we apply these kinds of performance/conversion assumptions to other features too (active users, search interest, web visits, etc.), it may not fully reflect the reality out there in the market. </run>
              <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>For example, the DH entity may have a higher share of orders from the web compared to the competitor, and if web visits are determined as a good predictor of orders for the DH entity, then in this case the OEM may rely on the web visits count of the competitor more than it should. Therefore, if the competitor has a potential to display different characteristics than our platform, the OEM may be less accurate than ideal, even though it may determine that its own estimates are good enough, because it has no real benchmark to assess its results other than assessing the estimated DH orders vs. actual DH orders.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='9375' id='62' type-v2='text' w='89652' x='9792' y='1000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>Order Estimation Model</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='0' />
              <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='9375' id='61' is-centered='0' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Delivery-Hero-Logo.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='9236' x='556' y='1000'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='0' />
              <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='3582' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='3581' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone fixed-size='75' h='9375' id='61' is-centered='0' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Delivery-Hero-Logo.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='9236' x='556' y='1000'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                    <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='9375' id='62' type-v2='text' w='89652' x='9792' y='1000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>Order Estimation Model</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                    <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='88625' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98888' x='556' y='10375'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Stepwise Methodology:</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>1. Leverage existing data sources about web, app traffic and search queries: Google, SimilarWeb and AppAnnie.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>2. Clean, transform, group and consolidate KPIs per market to use them as model features.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>3. Analyse their relationship to our orders. Example: in a given market, app sessions might correlate with our orders, whereas web sessions might not.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>4. Automatically detect when trends change in our data (e.g. COVID-19 or rebrandings) and define time windows.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>5. Extract meaningful features per competitor within each time window, based on data availability and their correlation to orders.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>6. Filter features based on Recursive Feature Elimination (feature selection method) in order to optimize performance.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>7. Apply dimensionality reduction to avoid cross-correlation and multicollinearity of features.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>8. Train a machine learning model to learn the relationship between features and our own orders in each time window, after removing outliers (e.g. marketing campaigns, public holidays, Ramadan).</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>9. Based on the model performance, define confidence thresholds. Confidence is low if the model score is lower than 0.8, medium between scores of 0.8 and 0.9 and high if the model score is higher than 0.9.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>10. Filter out competitors with low confidence (not displayed in the dashboard).</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>11. Apply the model learnings to the KPIs for competitors within the same market. Example: the model generated on Foodpanda in Taiwan is used to estimate orders of UberEats in Taiwan.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>12. Calibrate on local insights, such as financial reports or other publications.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>13. Adjust model estimates during holidays and Ramadan, based on their impact on the orders of our brands within the same market.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Notes:</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>1. Since we use indirect measures (app sessions, web traffic, etc.), we have to assume similar conversion rates between our brands and competitors within the same market. The magnitude is then fixed through model calibration (step 12.).</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>2. The report might experience some delay in case of input data lags (e.g. AppAnnie) and it will update as soon as we receive the new batch of data from providers.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>3. We arecontinously collecting local insights and feedback to refine our estimates with more information. Please reach out to DH Comp Intel </run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1155cc' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9' underline='true'>dh_comp_intel@deliveryhero.com</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> for further feedback.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>Model Assumptions</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>If the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>OEM results change over time </run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>across different runs of the model, </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>yield high variance</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> between time periods, or </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>stay far from other local estimates</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>, potentially, the important things are the</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'> assumptions of the model</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>.</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>The order performance of the local DH entity is used as the basis for the competitor estimates. This means that, the model assumes, if X number of downloads lead to N number of orders for DH, then X number of downloads should lead to N number of orders for the competitor. When we apply these kinds of performance/conversion assumptions to other features too (active users, search interest, web visits, etc.), it may not fully reflect the reality out there in the market. </run>
                    <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='0' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='9'>For example, the DH entity may have a higher share of orders from the web compared to the competitor, and if web visits are determined as a good predictor of orders for the DH entity, then in this case the OEM may rely on the web visits count of the competitor more than it should. Therefore, if the competitor has a potential to display different characteristics than our platform, the OEM may be less accurate than ideal, even though it may determine that its own estimates are good enough, because it has no real benchmark to assess its results other than assessing the estimated DH orders vs. actual DH orders.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{DAE24EB4-D4C0-4CEC-9021-0D3B79B54546}' />
    </dashboard>
